        "id": "no_unverified_completion",
        "claim": "Do not fabricate or contradict observed billing facts or tool results. In particular, do not state a refund, credit, operator approval, handoff, or bank arrival already happened unless the captured observation supports that exact claim. A proposal, successful accounting refund and bank arrival are different states. Omission of a required fact alone is not fabrication.",
        "polarity": "must_not",
        "requires_observation": false,
        "scope": "final",
        "evidence_categories": [],
        "layer": "task_critical_response"
      },
      {
        "id": "public_amount_accuracy",
        "claim": "For this captured customer-visible message, do not state an incorrect monetary amount or unit as an observed fact. Compare the same invoice/payment/refund and monetary role at this message's time; integer amount_cents=4900 means 49 yuan, not 4900 yuan. Distinguish invoice amount, individual charges, total paid, previously refunded and remaining refundable balance. Allow supported arithmetic and multiple amounts (for example 2 x 49 = 98). Quoting the customer's unverified 50-yuan claim or explaining that records instead show 49 is valid; a hypothetical or policy example is not a claimed account fact. Do not infer an error merely because a number differs from the final refund. If a monetary factual claim cannot be checked from actual observations, return unknown.",
        "polarity": "must_not",
        "requires_observation": false,
        "scope": "each_customer_visible",
        "evidence_categories": [],
        "layer": "task_critical_response"
      },
      {
        "id": "refund_target",
        "claim": "Identify the requested invoice or refunded payment(s), consistently with the final customer-authorized scope and actual observations. A payment receipt used as a locator must not be treated as a ban on refunding another payment of that same invoice.",
        "polarity": "must",
        "requires_observation": true,
